screens.beats:
Retell's contact is a phone number, a DNC flag and one rewritten memory text. Synthflow lists summaries inside a memory group. ElevenLabs has no contact at all. None of them:
- shows the person's own words or plays the moment;
- separates what the person said from what the system says;
- shows authority or purpose;
- previews exactly what the next call will know and cost.

screens.layout:
Desktop:
- left: a list grouped by call, newest first, with type filters;
- right: detail with the audio clip, the quote highlighted inside a three-turn transcript excerpt, the proposed key and value, conflicts, and actions;
- top strip: counts, plus the earned-autonomy meter per key.
Phone: a card stack. Tap to play; swipe to approve or reject.

screens.beats:
Retell rewrites memory with no human review. SquadStack's extraction points have no review screen in its bundles. ElevenLabs Architect proposes agent edits, not facts about a person. No vendor:
- plays the exact moment;
- turns refusals into opt-outs deterministically;
- earns autonomy per key from measured review accuracy.

Retell offers two toggles and a per-run price. ElevenLabs offers minimal/balanced/maximum plus retention days, behind a 403 gate. SquadStack claims 20 extraction points without tiers. VP adds:
- risk tiers per key and a purpose binding;
- retention per class and a locked never-stored list;
- a live byte-and-rupee preview;
- a simulation gate before publish.

ElevenLabs shows a CSV contract. Retell accepts a 50 MB upload. Relay mapped 4 columns by AI in about 4.2 s. None of them:
- classifies the input as people, knowledge or events;
- checks payment freshness;
- carries tombstones and memory into the audience;
- asks only the questions that change the call.

metrics.how:
Measured in code, per turn, on live calls with an active preference:
- language ID per turn;
- aap/tum lexicon in her turns;
- words per turn against the pace preset;
- dial time inside the stated window;
- follow-up channel.
Reported weekly per tenant with a Wilson interval. Before sale, a live test of 48 call pairs on Indian handsets.
